sentences.l:
There all the others perished, my good companions,
but I, the keel in my arms having taken, of the ship both-sides-curving,
nine-days was carried;

she, me having taken,
kindly loved and nurtured, and kept saying
she would make me immortal and ageless all my days;

And I, apart from the Zeus-fallen river,
having stepped out, in the bushes lay down to sleep, and around me leaves
I heaped up;

and she of a good thought did not at all fall short,
as you would not expect a younger person, having met you,
to do;

for she indeed bade me with her attendants follow,
but I was not willing, fearing and feeling shame,
lest in some way your heart too be angered, at the sight.
